{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>and they shall graze, etc.</b> Then the land of Judah will be a desolation, and sheep shall graze in it as though they were accustomed to being there." "<b>[as their portion].</b> From an Aramaic root, and like it is דוברו' בים (1 Kings 5:23)." "<b>fattened ones.</b> These are the fat sheep that have מוח in them, and like it is ממוחים (Isaiah 25:6). And חרבות is from the root חרבן. It is in construct state and the word הארץ is missing, like ושכור' (Isaiah 51:21) יגון ולא מיין, משא חמור להם (Exodus 1:14?). The meaning of גרים: strangers who will dwell there shall eat. Now, מחים is an attribute of a noun, and they are פעולים, while הגרים are פועלים."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The bracketed lemma and verse reference follow the Hebrew; the precise form cited is uncertain.", 2 "The Exodus citation 'שמות א' ט\"ו כ\"' appears corrupt; the referenced phrase משא חמור להם does not occur in Exodus 1:14, and the verse number may be in error."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:02.687747180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}